        "id": "ch10_5-1",
        "text": "Summary\nIn this chapter, we emphasized the importance of disaster recovery planning, backup and restore\nstrategies, and troubleshooting various system issues. Every system administrator should be able to\nput their knowledge into practice when disaster strikes. Different types of failures will eventually hit\nthe running servers, so solutions should be found as soon as possible to ensure minimal downtime\nand to prevent data loss.\nThis chapter represented the culmination of the Advanced Linux Administration section of this book.\nIn the next chapter, we will introduce you to server administration , with emphasis on KVM virtual\nmachine management, Docker containers, and different types of Linux server configuration.\nDisaster Recovery, Diagnostics, and Troubleshooting\n414",
